Correctness fixes Minecraft 26.2's server needs, wrong at 9be5eca57 (the first is still wrong on TeaVM master):
  VirtualTableBuilder.copyEntries took the first implementor any ancestor table offered, so a class inheriting an
  interface default through its superclass (AbstractMap -> Map.computeIfAbsent) kept it even when it implements a
  more specific interface that overrides it (ConcurrentMap.computeIfAbsent): Guava's MapMakerInternalMap then ran
  Map's default, which calls put, which dispatched to AbstractMap.put and threw (ResourceKey.create, at bootstrap).
  An interface default now yields to a default of a more specific interface; a class method is never displaced.
  TConcurrentMap.computeIfAbsent returned putIfAbsent's result (the previous value: null on insertion) instead of
  the value now mapped.
  Upstream 7883fc417 (ConcurrentHashMap.computeIfAbsent/computeIfPresent on null results), backported.
  DecimalFormat refused a negative subpattern without digits (JOML's " 0.000E0;-"); the JDK accepts a prefix alone.
  The linear-memory target flagged WeakReference / ReferenceQueue with the GC's reference types without reshaping them
  into its layout (only the C target does), so the first collection over a WeakReference trapped. No VM type there
  now: references are strong, as that target's classlib already implemented them.
Codegen: changes which method a virtual call reaches where the old table was wrong; nothing else.

